HST Office: Writer and shared character/paragraph/page/border/area dialogs laid out per the dialog layout rulebook.

- Tab pages get a 12 px margin (page root border-width 12; tabbed dialog shells keep 6); dialogs without tabs get 12.
  The page-border tab adds its own 12 px around the Art/Width/Apply-to row, as its embedded border page has it.
- Paragraph > Alignment: the six alignment choices in two columns (Start/Center/End, Left/Right/Justified), the
  justify options under Justified; the Paragraph dialog fits a 1366x768 screen at 100 % again.
- Page Style: the inner Margins/Paper/Layout pages get a 12 px margin; Layout combo boxes keep their natural width;
  Header/Footer check boxes span both columns so the spin buttons sit next to their labels; Footnote area labels
  of both groups share one width so the values line up.
- Labels start-aligned (Word Count names, Drop Caps, Text Flow, Transparency); the Description label sits on the
  first line of its text box; no ellipsized labels (Header height, numbering options).
- Table of Contents entry structure: 4 px between the token buttons and text pieces.
- Fields > Document: the type list is a third wider so translated type names are not cut.
No widget id, handler, string, mnemonic, tab order or accessibility relation changes.

